course: dictionary
lesson: 3275
title: Running an errand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An errand is a short trip to do a small job. You might buy something, deliver something or take a message. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «She was sent on an errand to the shop» tells you that someone went out to do a small job.
explain: Children often run errands for parents or neighbours, like posting a letter or buying milk. «Run errands» means doing several of these small jobs. Ask yourself: what would fit in the sentence instead of errand? A job, a trip, a message? If your meaning still makes sense, you are probably right.
explain: In a story, a character sent on an errand often meets an adventure on the way. The errand gives the hero a reason to leave home. The sentence «She imagines Dinah sending her "on messages" (errands)» shows that the writer explains the word in brackets, so the reader can understand it.
fact: An errand is a short trip to do a small job.
fact: Errands can be buying something, delivering something or taking a message.
fact: Useful phrases are «run an errand», «go on an errand» and «run errands».
fact: The brackets in «on messages» (errands) show that messages means errands in that sentence.
fact: In stories, a character sent on an errand often meets an adventure.
exercise: «She imagines Dinah sending her "on messages" (errands).» What do the brackets tell you? | It is a question to answer | It is a rude word | *Messages here means errands | It is the end of the story
exercise: Ana runs errands for her neighbour, posting letters and buying milk. What is an errand? | A long holiday abroad | A big party | *A short trip to do a small job | A tricky puzzle
exercise: Which phrase means to do a small job for someone? | Paint an errand | *Run an errand | Lose an errand | Break an errand
test: Mum asks you to go to the shop for milk and post a letter on the way. What kind of job is this? | A puzzle | A parade | A dream | *An errand
test: What does the word errand mean? | A long journey across the sea | A type of cake | *A short trip to do a small job | A loud argument
exam: Dad says, "Can you run an errand for me before tea?" What does he want you to do? | *Make a short trip to do a small job | Sleep early | Write a story | Paint the fence
